# Line endings are a property of this repo, not of the machine that cloned it.
#
# Without this, a Windows clone (core.autocrlf defaults to true there, including on the
# GitHub Actions windows runners) checks every source file out as CRLF, while .editorconfig
# asks for LF - so `dotnet format --verify-no-changes` fails on every line of every file,
# on Windows only, with a tree nobody touched. Pin it here and the two agree everywhere.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Visual Studio rewrites the solution with CRLF and a UTF-8 BOM every time it touches it.
# It is stored that way; leave it exactly as-is rather than fight it on every checkout.
*.sln -text

# Batch is CRLF's native habitat - a label or goto can misbehave with bare LF.
*.bat text eol=crlf

# Never munge these.
*.ico binary
*.png binary
*.exe binary
*.zip binary
